From ced311a28d3115a80eb8983dceb2384d460fb403 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RDoom <171243930+aeon1911@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:33:16 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 47/54] Switch: smoke and fire in a half-resolution layer
 blended over the scene

Large translucent effect sprites (alpha or additive, NXIsPureEffect, at
least rd_halfeffects_minarea of the screen) of the main view go to
GLDL_NXEFFECTS. When they cover rd_halfeffects_minscreen (0.6) screens or
more, they are drawn after the translucent list into an RGBA8 layer of half
the resolution and blended over the scene before the weapon and HUD.

- layer cleared to (0,0,0,1); FXLAYER pipelines (ColorMask bit 0x100, same
  key size so old warm lists stay valid) keep in alpha how much of the
  scene shows through; composite = scene * a + rgb (PP pass like SSAO's)
- layer depth: scene depth copied to R32F at half size by a PP draw
  (nxdepth.fp, texelFetch), then written through gl_FragDepth by a small
  depth-only pass; the scene depth is sampled (DS|SAMPLED, ZCULL as with
  rd_vk_zcull 1)
- the depth copy is read back in the first frames: all zero (Ryujinx
  cannot sample NVK's depth views, "Invalid texture format 0x2512B") turns
  the layer off for the session, effects then drawn as before
- composite/depth pipelines, shaders and images prepared at level load
- perf.log: effects in the layer and their screen area per frame
- rd_vk_halfeffects (on), rd_halfeffects_debug test modes

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
